Build succeeded. The component is ready. Here's how to use it:

```razor
<UserActivityTracker TimeoutSeconds="120" OnIdle="HandleIdle" OnActive="HandleActive">
    <p>Your app content here</p>
</UserActivityTracker>

@code {
    private Task HandleIdle() { /* user went idle */ return Task.CompletedTask; }
    private Task HandleActive() { /* user came back */ return Task.CompletedTask; }
}
```

**How it works:**
- A colocated JS module listens for `mousemove`, `keydown`, `click`, and `scroll` on the wrapper `<div>`
- A timeout fires `OnIdle` after the configured inactivity period
- Any subsequent activity fires `OnActive` and resets the timer
- `IAsyncDisposable` ensures the JS timer and event listeners are cleaned up on removal
